    "damping_LCDM_e^-2tau_reion": 0.8976275964304349,
    "assessment": "The Step-16 broad tail was dominated by the closure choice n_e = 5000 n_b0 beyond the edge: it carries 36.8% of the kernel over z > 1080. Because that zone scatters at ~11 Thomson depths per L0, folding in absorption only suppresses it when the edge destroys photons faster than they scatter free \u2014 at kappa=1000/L0 the post-edge weight falls to 0.2% and the wall carries ~87%; at kappa=1/L0 the tail still carries 35%.  A thermalization edge must satisfy the large-kappa condition by definition (absorption outrunning scatter escape is what makes a boundary thermalize); the quantitative requirement on the Gate-11B absorption model is kappa_abs >> 11/L0.  What remains in the forward direction is a thin foreground screen: under the thermalized-edge kernel the wing carries 8% of the renormalized weight (the tau_reion datum, identical in observable role to the standard reionization tail) and the trough 4%.  The effective primary-anisotropy damping is e^{-2 tau_fg} = 0.85 versus the standard 0.90 \u2014 the same order and the same degenerate direction as the measured tau_reion screen.",
