    "assessment": "The transit calculation is now integrated over the burst window in particle fluence; an earlier draft integrated the whole collapse at burst luminosity (overcounting fluence for tau_b < t_ff), omitted the 1/E_nu factor in y_n, and hardcoded the tau_b >= t_ff fraction at unity.  The corrected result: for tau_b <=~ t_ff the strongly-irradiated envelope fraction reaches ~0.28-1.00 at E_nu=1e58 (median boost vs static ~40-4e4), far above the static enclosed fraction ~2e-5-0.016 \u2014 shells descending through the burst are exposed at radii far below r_crit.  For tau_b >> t_ff the luminosity dilutes and the exposure relaxes toward the static bound; raising E_nu to 1e59-1e60 closes the remaining deficit across the grid.  What remains undetermined is which irradiated shells are ejected rather than retained \u2014 the channel's ejecta identity still requires a dynamical bounce/ejection model; the irradiation side is now bounded rather than open.",
